  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 1245 AM CDT Tue Oct 13 2026\n\nFriday through Wednesday:\n\nThe main focus for Friday will be the wind as a strong high\npressure nudges in behind the departing low and bring a fairly\nsignificant pressure gradient across the area through the day\nFriday. Winds will be expected to approach Wind Advisory \ncriteria, primarily near the shoreline areas, where NNW wind \ngusts may approach 45-50mph. In addition, cooler conditions may\nmake for a bit of a wind chill, relative to the temperatures,\nprimarily Friday morning when apparent temperatures may reach\nthe mid 30s. \n\nWinds will lighten back up as the high moves overhead into\nSaturday but the rapid departure of the high and impinging low\npressure to the north will bring back breezy conditions from the\nsouthwest later Saturday into Sunday. Since this front and the\nassociated low will swing off to the northeast the front is\nexpected to weaken to the point of dissipation and lighter winds\nwill return a higher pressure builds back into the region for\nMonday. Uncertainty definitely increases early to mid next week\nbut the general trend is for drier weather until at least\nmidweek.\n\nKuroski",
